# Orient here first

- `ROADMAP.md` — where the project is: done, in flight, next, parked, and why. Read this first.
- `CLAUDE.md` — how the codebase works. Architecture, invariants, gotchas.
- `.plans/NN-*.md` — one initiative each. The `**Status.**` block at the top of a plan is the source
  of truth for that initiative.
- `.plans/37-config-format-decision.md` — script language / config UX: JSON `@PANEL_START`; drop
  Configuration code tab; migrate remaining DSF panels. HTML/JSX skin deferred. **Next: cleanup +
  panel consistency (go-ahead 2026-08-28; priority call 2026-08-31).** Read before touching
  `@PANEL_START`, `@CONFIG_START`, `src/config-ui/parser.js`, or the Configuration code tab.
- `.plans/38-script-storage-variables.md` — script storage & sharing: Variables + LocalStorage
  (both keep); library edit UX deferred for a consistent model. Read before changing how user
  scripts are saved, loaded, or shared.
- `.plans/39-foundation-maintenance.md` — DSF metadata hygiene on plugin open; Foundation config
  script removed. Ambiguous stamp collisions still deferred. Manifest-preserving copy/move is
  part of config cleanup consistency. Read before changing `readFoundation` /
  `reconcileFoundation` repair behaviour or plugin boot cleanup.
- **Do not commit `.plans/`.** They are gitignored and stay local. Update `ROADMAP.md` when a plan
  moves.
- **Ramp recognition is deferred** — manifest load + recreate is enough; do not prioritise it.
- **Library / non-persistable edit UX is deferred** — one model later for remotes, DSF, utilities,
  `@` libs; do not ship a library-only banner.
- `DEFERRED.md` — known problems left unfixed, with what fixing involves. Check before reporting
  something as new.
- `CHANGELOG.md` — what changed, in behaviour terms.

**The repo is the shared state.** Work happens across more than one tool. A decision that is not
written into one of the files above did not happen. When something moves, update its plan's status
and `ROADMAP.md` in the same pass.

# Standing rules

- Nothing is committed unless Márton asks.
- Backward compatibility with saved user scripts is not negotiable. They live in `clientStorage`
  today; the planned model is STRING variables (`.plans/38`). Until migration ships, treat
  `clientStorage` as canonical. A change that alters behaviour for a script with none of the new
  regions is a stop-and-report.
- A Figma number comes from inside Figma. No Node substitute presented as a measurement.
- Click what you built, in Figma, with a real collection loaded. Field reads and passing tests have
  hidden three separate bugs that one click would have found.
- The preview strip is the instrument for colour bugs. Hex values, before and after.
- Panel copy goes through `.claude/skills/ux-copy/SKILL.md`.
- `npm run build:production` disables the dev bridge. Run `npm run build:dev` after.
